# SPARQL Error Correction Prompt

You are an expert in semantic web and SPARQL query generation.

Instructions:
- You are given an error message from GraphDB and the previous SPARQL query.
- Analyze the error and fix the SPARQL query accordingly.
- Use the extracted clause data, relevant IRIs, and Turtle data below for context.
- Strictly follow the predicate and class naming conventions as shown in the Turtle data.
- Only use prefixes and endpoints that are present in the Turtle data block below. Do not invent or use any other prefixes/endpoints.
- Output only the corrected SPARQL query. Do not include any explanation or commentary.

### User Query
Who makes the most products? Include ties.

### Error message from GraphDB
Response:
Response:
Response:
b'MALFORMED QUERY: Encountered " "max" "MAX "" at line 17, column 12.\r\nWas expecting one of:\r\n    "(" ...\r\n    "*" ...\r\n    "distinct" ...\r\n    "reduced" ...\r\n    <VAR1> ...\r\n    <VAR2> ...\r\n    '
All retries failed.

### Previous SPARQL query
PREFIX iof-core: <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/Core/>
PREFIX sdk: <http://asu.edu/semantics/SUDOKN/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

SELECT ?man ?label ?productCount
WHERE {
  {
    SELECT ?man (COUNT(DISTINCT ?prod) AS ?productCount) ?label
    WHERE {
      ?man a iof-core:Manufacturer .
      ?man sdk:manufactures ?prod .
      OPTIONAL { ?man rdfs:label ?label . }
    }
    GROUP BY ?man ?label
  }
  {
    SELECT MAX(?c) AS ?maxCount WHERE {
      {
        SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?pp) AS ?c)
        WHERE {
          ?m2 a iof-core:Manufacturer ;
              sdk:manufactures ?pp .
        }
        GROUP BY ?m2
      }
    }
  }
  FILTER(?productCount = ?maxCount)
}
ORDER BY DESC(?productCount)

